IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `rda-priority-caveats`

-- Registration of Deeds Act 1988, ss 8 and 14 to 16 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been
-- checked against a decided case or the rules under the Act (none were retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_rda.py), so that a typing slip
-- cannot make a case say something other than its name. Expected results were written by hand from the text.

§ `Fixtures`

`a purchaser's caveat in proper form` MEANS CaveatFacts WITH
    `it discloses an estate or interest in land` IS TRUE
    `it states the Government survey lot number` IS TRUE
    `it affects only part of a lot` IS FALSE
    `it clearly identifies that part in an annexed plan` IS FALSE
    `the claim is in fact justified` IS TRUE
    `notice was served by registered post on the proprietor and prior claimants` IS TRUE
    `years since registration` IS 1
    `withdrawn by the caveator` IS FALSE
    `cancelled by order of court` IS FALSE

`a groundless caveat in proper form never notified` MEANS CaveatFacts WITH
    `it discloses an estate or interest in land` IS TRUE
    `it states the Government survey lot number` IS TRUE
    `it affects only part of a lot` IS FALSE
    `it clearly identifies that part in an annexed plan` IS FALSE
    `the claim is in fact justified` IS FALSE
    `notice was served by registered post on the proprietor and prior claimants` IS FALSE
    `years since registration` IS 1
    `withdrawn by the caveator` IS FALSE
    `cancelled by order of court` IS FALSE

`a caveat disclosing no interest` MEANS CaveatFacts WITH
